   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^{n+1}(x - 4)^{n}}{n\\,10^{n}} \\) for \\( |x - 4| < 10 \\). The sum of the first three terms of this series at \\( x = 5 \\) is used to approximate \\( f(5) \\). Find the alternating series error bound for this approximation."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         40000
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At \\( x = 5 \\), \\( x - 4 = 1 \\), so the terms are \\( (-1)^{n+1} a_n \\) with \\( a_n = \\frac{(\\frac{1}{10})^{n}}{n} \\). These alternate in sign and decrease in absolute value to 0.",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The approximation uses terms \\( n = 1 \\) to \\( n = 3 \\), so the first omitted term is the one with \\( n = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Its absolute value is \\( a_{4} = \\frac{1}{40000} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            40000
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "By the alternating series error bound, the error is at most \\( \\frac{1}{40000} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            40000
         ]
      }
   ],
